.page jukebox 1 Reimu's Jukebox, the music player

# SYNOPSIS
*jukebox* [*-p*] [*--trace*] [_FILE_ | _DIRECTORY_ ...]
*jukebox* *--list*

# DESCRIPTION
`jukebox` is the desktop's music player. Its window is the Prismriver Concert Hall: Lunasa, Merlin and Lyrica stand on a stage and play whatever the playlist holds, and the three of them jump to the low, middle and high parts of the sound while a row of bars in the orchestra pit shows its spectrum. The playlist on the left is made of the songs that ship with the system (`/ScarletDevilMansion/share/music`, see tms(5)) followed by the `.wav` and `.tms` files in `~/Music`; files named on the command line come first, and *Open music...* adds more. WAV files may be 8, 16, 24 or 32 bits, mono or stereo, at any rate.

Below the stage are the title and mood of the song, a seek bar with the time, the buttons (previous, play and pause, stop, next) and the master volume. The volume is the one of the whole machine, the same as `volume(1)` and the speaker in the panel. When the playlist ends it starts again unless *Repeat* is off.

The sound goes through `/dev/audio` like any other program's, so the Jukebox can play while other programs beep. Without a sound device the window still opens, says so, and cannot play.

# OPTIONS
@ *-p*
    Start playing at once.
@ *--trace*
    Print a line on standard output for each thing that happens (`jukebox: playing ...`, `paused at ...`, `seek ...`, `volume ...`).
@ *--list*
    Print the playlist (number, title, length, file) and exit; no window.

# KEYS
@ Space
    Play or pause. Enter plays the selected song, double click does too.
@ S, N, P
    Stop, next, previous (P restarts a song that has played for a few seconds).
@ Left, Right
    Five seconds back or forward. Clicking the seek bar jumps there.
@ Up, Down, Home, End
    Move through the playlist.
@ Ctrl+Up, Ctrl+Down, M
    Louder, quieter, mute.
@ R, Ctrl+O, Ctrl+Q, F1
    Repeat on or off, open a file, quit, about.

# EXIT STATUS
0 normally; 1 if there is no window server; 2 for a usage error.

# SEE ALSO
play(1), volume(1), tms(5), audio(7)
